 "result": "The last commit, `67044bf` (\"retry longer; lower tax on big orders\"), changed two functions in two files.\n\n**1. `tax(price)` in `calc/pricing.py`**\n- **Before:** every price was taxed at `TAX_RATE`, which is 0.08 (8%).\n- **After:** prices under 1000 still pay 8%. Prices of 1000 or more pay 5% instead, which is hardcoded as `0.05` rather than kept in a named constant.\n- **Side effect:** tax now drops at the 1000 line. A price of 999.99 is taxed 80.00, while 1000 is taxed only 50.00.\n\n**2. `backoff(attempt)` in `calc/upload.py`**\n- **Before:** the wait between upload retries doubled each time (`2 ** attempt` seconds) but never went above 30 seconds.\n- **After:** the limit is now 60 seconds. `upload()` waits this long between attempts, and the retry count is still `MAX_UPLOAD_RETRIES` (7 by default). So later retries wait up to twice as long, and a run that fails every time takes noticeably longer before giving up.\n\nNothing else in the code changed.",
